245:                Reconfigures autoescape behavior.  The default is 'auto' which means that \
246-                the file extension sets the auto escaping mode.  A single final .j2, .jinja, \
247-                or .jinja2 suffix is ignored, so report.html.jinja2 uses HTML escaping.  \
248-                Suffixes are matched without regard to ASCII letter case.  The extensions \
249-                .htm, .html, .xml, and .xhtml use HTML escaping; .json, .json5, .yaml, and \
250-                .yml use JSON escaping.  Other extensions disable escaping.\n\n\
251-                \
252-                html means that variables are escaped to HTML5 and XML rules.  json means \
253-                that output is safe for both JSON and YAML rules (eg: strings are formatted \
254-                as JSON strings etc.).  none disables escaping entirely.  These explicit \
255-                modes override filename detection.\n\n\
